   "html_text": "Another issue Nāgārjuna raises (in MMK 9:3) concerns the epistemic status of the self. A tension arises once we note that in its role as a unifier of our cognitive life a substantial self features in all our experiences, as the subject having the experiences, but at the same time, given the distinctness of such a self from our body and all parts of our mental life it must also be distinct from all experiences. In order to have epistemic access to our self it must be able to function as a cogniti",
